From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:43:45 +0000
Subject: ACPI: thermal: make SSTP optional

Some Sky1 firmware has thermal zones but no SSTP method. The zones then
fail to register, and the board has no thermal zones. Register the zones
without SSTP. IPA then estimates the sustainable power.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/acpi/thermal.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/acpi/thermal.c b/drivers/acpi/thermal.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/acpi/thermal.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/thermal.c
@@ -986,9 +986,9 @@ static int acpi_thermal_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		pr_warn(FW_BUG "No valid trip points!\n");
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_CIX_THERMAL
-	result = acpi_thermal_get_sustainable_power(tz);
-	if (result)
-		return result;
+	/* SSTP is optional: without it, IPA estimates the sustainable power. */
+	if (acpi_thermal_get_sustainable_power(tz))
+		acpi_handle_debug(device->handle, "No SSTP, sustainable power unknown\n");
 #endif
 
 	result = acpi_thermal_register_thermal_zone(tz, trip_table,
-- 
Armbian

